Charge the MiniLoong Pocket1 at its full input current.

The board routes VBUS only to the rk817, so the USB PHY never classifies the
charger and the PMIC plug-in fallback holds every source to the 450mA
USB-port limit - about 1.7W, slow enough that charging barely outpaces use.
Opt into the AC-limit fallback so it charges at max_input_current (1.5A).

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miniloong.dts	2026-09-27 12:19:14.873294373 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miniloong.dts	2026-09-27 12:19:14.886295451 +0200
@@ -1009,6 +1009,14 @@
 			extcon = <&usb2phy0>;
 			rockchip,validate-charger-with-pmic-plugin;
 			rockchip,pmic-plugin-usb-fallback;
+			/*
+			 * VBUS only reaches the PMIC on this board, so the USB PHY
+			 * never classifies the charger and every source would be
+			 * held to the 450mA USB-port limit. Charge at the
+			 * max_input_current instead; min_input_voltage makes the
+			 * rk817 back off if a weak source such as a PC port sags.
+			 */
+			rockchip,pmic-plugin-fallback-ac;
 		};
 
 		rk817_codec: codec {
